# Cloudflare's, for every file of the wallet it serves (wrangler.jsonc), at
# its address under /wallet/. It reads this file and doesn't serve it. What no
# file answers, deploy/worker.js does, with the same.
#
# No fuller Content-Security-Policy yet. One would need at least script-src
# 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' with the hashes of SvelteKit's inline start
# scripts (kit.csp can write them); style-src 'unsafe-inline', for Svelte's
# transitions and AppKit; connect-src for the node (https: and wss:),
# DuskEVM's RPC, its L1 RPC and explorer, the EVM RPCs in the networks file,
# CoinGecko, the names API, and Reown's API, RPC and relay (wss:); img-src
# data: and Reown's icons; and frame-src for WalletConnect's verify frame.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/wallet/_app/immutable/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
